    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Step 1: Convert all the units to centimeters.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"12\\cancel{{{\\text{millimeters}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{1{\\text{ }}\\cancel{{{\\text{meter}}}}}}{{{\\text{1,0}}\\cancel{{{\\text{00}}}}\\cancel{{{\\text{millimeter}}}}}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{\\cancel{{100}}{\\text{ centimeters}}}}{{1{\\text{ }}\\cancel{{{\\text{meter}}}}}}} \\right) = 1.2{\\text{ centimeters}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Find the volume of a box.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"V{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}L{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}W \\times H{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}\\left( {{\\text{1}}{\\text{.2 cm}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{5 cm}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{1}}{\\text{.7 cm}}} \\right){\\text{ }} = 10.2{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^3}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 3: Convert the volume of a box into milliliters.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"10.2\\cancel{{{\\text{cubic centimeters}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{{\\text{ 1 milliliter}}}}{{{\\text{ 1}}\\cancel{{{\\text{cubic centimeter}}}}}}} \\right) = 10.2{\\text{ milliliters}}\"></span></p>\n"
    },
    {
